{"article_ids": ["c10310cdcfd4a8e4"], "canonical_title": "UniPipe: Unified Inference Serving and Fine-Tuning for Deadline-Constrained DNN Surrogate Workflows", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.62, "description": "The paper presents UniPipe, a system that combines real‑time inference serving with on‑the‑fly fine‑tuning of deep neural network (DNN) surrogates used in high‑rate scientific workflows, such as ptychographic imaging at next‑generation X‑ray light sources. The approach aims to keep surrogate accuracy as input distributions drift while meeting strict latency deadlines, offering 100‑1000× higher throughput than traditional iterative solvers.", "entities": ["term:dnn"], "first_seen": "2026-11-13T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_c10310cdcfd4a8e4", "importance_score": 6.34, "last_updated": "2026-11-13T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-lg"]}
{"article_ids": ["5b69826eead48a96", "d6d23163b98ddfa1", "341363dd4020e2e5", "963b6a1992f174a9", "d7e80ea809e6c296", "d7c21c501eb23f12", "aeee01f562824dca"], "canonical_title": "Introducing Gemini 4 Hydrogen", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "Google released the Gemini 4 Hydrogen large‑language model and integrated it into Google Search’s AI Mode, the Gemini app and all user tiers. The model is described as better at understanding multi‑part questions, typo‑laden queries and highly specific requests, surfacing relevant links and providing richer visual responses.", "entities": ["model:gemini", "model:gemini-0.37", "model:gemini-4", "org:google", "term:ui", "term:url"], "first_seen": "2026-11-12T18:00:00Z", "id": "evt_5b69826eead48a96", "importance_score": 6.27, "last_updated": "2026-11-12T22:55:19Z", "source_ids": ["google-deepmind", "google-ai", "techcrunch-ai", "the-verge-ai", "hacker-news", "simon-willison"]}
{"article_ids": ["405dc9f5cf29c191"], "canonical_title": "FIBER: Bayesian Fusion of Fast-DetectGPT and IRT-Informed Detector Evidence for LLM-Generated Text Detection", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "Researchers released FIBER, a method that combines continuous Fast-DetectGPT scores with outputs from other detectors using IRT-informed Bayesian evidence recalibration. The approach aims to improve detection of LLM‑generated text across domain and generator shifts, addressing poor generalization of supervised detectors and limitations of zero‑shot methods that rely on single statistical signals.", "entities": ["term:fiber", "term:irt"], "first_seen": "2026-11-13T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_405dc9f5cf29c191", "importance_score": 6.19, "last_updated": "2026-11-13T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["0ca05117dff37c92"], "canonical_title": "How Natera designed an agentic AI system for lab ops with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "Natera built SWARM, an agentic AI system using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore that captures institutional lab‑operations knowledge, deploys it at scale, and reports a 130× faster first‑response time and 96.2% automated coverage of support tickets.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "term:swarm"], "first_seen": "2026-11-12T21:47:07Z", "id": "evt_0ca05117dff37c92", "importance_score": 6.04, "last_updated": "2026-11-12T21:47:07Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["9e5328de36564d89"], "canonical_title": "Termination Lag: Coding Agents Solve Early but Stop Late", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "Researchers introduced the concept of \"termination lag,\" the gap between a coding agent's first correct patch and when it stops execution. They measured this across five models, two agent frameworks, and three SWE-bench datasets, recording every distinct repository patch. Their analysis found that 38‑82% of successful runs produced a correct solution on the initial patch but kept running afterward.", "entities": ["term:swe"], "first_seen": "2026-11-13T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_9e5328de36564d89", "importance_score": 5.49, "last_updated": "2026-11-13T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
